WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.502
This is the learning path for Module 6.

00:00:02.502 --> 00:00:04.472
We start with imports.

00:00:04.472 --> 00:00:10.647
An import lets us bring tools from another Python file or library into our current program.

00:00:10.647 --> 00:00:15.562
This is important because we do not want to rewrite common tools every time.

00:00:15.562 --> 00:00:17.857
Next, we look at your own module.

00:00:17.857 --> 00:00:22.557
A module can simply be a Python file that contains reusable code.

00:00:22.557 --> 00:00:27.342
You can place helper functions in one file and import them into another file.

00:00:27.342 --> 00:00:32.892
Then we discuss packages. A package is a folder that groups related modules.

00:00:32.892 --> 00:00:36.097
You can think of it as a larger organizational unit.

00:00:36.097 --> 00:00:38.617
After that, we move into classes.

00:00:38.617 --> 00:00:41.562
A class is a blueprint for creating objects.

00:00:41.562 --> 00:00:44.772
This is the beginning of object-oriented programming.

00:00:44.772 --> 00:00:47.302
Then we study objects and methods.

00:00:47.302 --> 00:00:53.422
An object is one specific instance of a class, and a method is a function that belongs to

00:00:53.422 --> 00:00:54.867
that object. Finally, we discuss design choices.

00:00:54.867 --> 00:00:56.892
Sometimes a function is enough.

00:00:56.892 --> 00:00:58.967
Sometimes a dictionary is enough.

00:00:58.967 --> 00:01:01.117
Sometimes a class is useful.

00:01:01.117 --> 00:01:07.347
The goal is to choose the simplest structure that makes the code clear.

00:01:07.347 --> 00:01:10.357
This module is not only about syntax.

00:01:10.357 --> 00:01:14.411
It is about thinking like a programmer who wants to build code that can grow.
